WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.561
Imagine I was holding a 1.5 volt battery

00:00:02.561 --> 00:00:03.661
one of those batteries that

00:00:03.671 --> 00:00:05.860
you put into a camera. One of the teeny ones.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:09.280
And I ran four hundred miles of

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.011
wire from this battery down to Los Angeles.

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:14.651
This shark could sense the electrical

00:00:14.651 --> 00:00:17.021
field off of that battery 400 miles away.

00:00:17.021 --> 00:00:20.641
So this sense is 5 million times more

00:00:20.641 --> 00:00:22.841
sensitive than any human sense. It is

00:00:22.841 --> 00:00:25.521
by far the most sensitive sense we've ever

00:00:25.521 --> 00:00:28.161
discovered on the planet. So the next time

00:00:28.181 --> 00:00:29.821
you're swimming at the Dolphin Club,

00:00:29.821 --> 00:00:32.821
you can remember that sharks aren't really

00:00:32.831 --> 00:00:35.500
smelling you. They're honing in on your

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.741
electroreceptive field that is coming

00:00:38.741 --> 00:00:40.901
off of your heart and brain waves.

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:42.201
So it was a pretty frightening thought

00:00:42.201 --> 00:00:43.961
when I learned that. Because I surf

00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:46.521
down at Ocean Beach all the time.

00:00:46.521 --> 00:00:50.561
Anyway, sharks do it. Bees do it. Birds do it.

00:00:50.561 --> 00:00:55.081
We probably do it, too. Humans have probably

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:57.611
been using some sort of magneto-receptive

00:00:57.611 --> 00:01:01.211
sense for centuries. Ancient Polynesian

00:01:01.211 --> 00:01:03.401
sailors could navigate hundreds of miles

00:01:03.401 --> 00:01:05.921
across open ocean and usually always

00:01:05.921 --> 00:01:08.881
make it back to the same exact spot.

00:01:08.891 --> 00:01:10.900
Now they could use celestial navigation

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.571
for some of the time. Solar navigation for

00:01:13.571 --> 00:01:15.641
some of that other time. But they couldn't

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:17.501
use both all of the times, especially during

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:20.431
stormy weather. So how did they do it?

00:01:20.431 --> 00:01:23.290
Then there's these guys: the

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:26.290
Guugu Yimithirr, an Australian aboriginal tribe.

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:29.021
They incorporated cardinal directions

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:31.451
into their language. They didn't have

00:01:31.451 --> 00:01:34.510
words for right, left, forward, or

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:36.521
backwards. But they did have words

00:01:36.521 --> 00:01:39.461
for North, South, East, and West. If one of

00:01:39.461 --> 00:01:41.171
these guys wanted you to make room

00:01:41.171 --> 00:01:43.150
for him on a bench, he wouldn't ask you to

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.010
to move over to the right. He would ask you

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:48.311
to move south. They didn't bend backwards.

00:01:48.311 --> 00:01:51.610
They bent eastwards or northwards.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:55.101
The only way this group could communicate

00:01:55.101 --> 00:01:57.760
was if they knew their exact position

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.951
on the globe at all times. Which is a

00:01:59.951 --> 00:02:02.771
very hard thing to do at night and

00:02:02.771 --> 00:02:04.401
a very hard thing to do in an

00:02:04.401 --> 00:02:07.141
enclosed space. But they weren't alone

00:02:07.141 --> 00:02:09.741
dozens and dozens of cultures also

00:02:09.741 --> 00:02:13.181
used Cardinal languages. Just like these guys

00:02:13.181 --> 00:02:16.491
the Tzeltal of central Mexico they again

00:02:16.491 --> 00:02:18.111
didn't have words for right or left but

00:02:18.111 --> 00:02:20.061
they had words for north south east and

00:02:20.061 --> 00:02:24.381
west. In the 01990s a bunch of researchers

00:02:24.381 --> 00:02:26.861
took one of these Tzeltal speakers and

00:02:26.861 --> 00:02:29.841
placed him in a room. They blindfolded him

00:02:29.841 --> 00:02:31.621
and they spun him around about

00:02:31.621 --> 00:02:34.001
25 times and immediately asked them

00:02:34.001 --> 00:02:35.941
to identify where north south east and west was.

00:02:35.941 --> 00:02:38.541
This guy did it without any hesitation.

00:02:38.541 --> 00:02:41.061
20 times in a row. And I

00:02:41.061 --> 00:02:43.841
think they just gave up and moved on after that.

00:02:44.401 --> 00:02:48.201
You know, thank God for the 70s:

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:50.301
here's a picture from some 70s

00:02:50.301 --> 00:02:53.841
experiments. In the 70s and 80s, human

00:02:53.841 --> 00:02:56.841
magneto reception was all the rage.

00:02:56.841 --> 00:02:59.751
They conducted over 1,000 experiments in this

00:02:59.751 --> 00:03:04.341
stuff and almost all the time people

00:03:04.341 --> 00:03:06.761
who were blindfolded, twisted around,

00:03:06.761 --> 00:03:09.021
magnets on their head, whatever, they were able

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:11.871
to point in their home direction. With

00:03:11.871 --> 00:03:14.840
one exception. When the experimenters would

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.181
tape a little piece of magnetite

00:03:17.181 --> 00:03:19.101
to their foreheads they lost all sense of

00:03:19.101 --> 00:03:21.831
direction. Now researchers had done this

00:03:21.831 --> 00:03:24.141
years before they had taken a turtle

00:03:24.141 --> 00:03:26.661
and they had taken a bird, and taped...

00:03:26.661 --> 00:03:27.861
I'm not talking about a kitchen magnet

00:03:27.861 --> 00:03:29.631
I'm talking about a teeny teeny piece.

00:03:29.631 --> 00:03:31.731
And it's really sad, if you ever see these

00:03:31.731 --> 00:03:33.531
videos, because the turtles just kind of swim

00:03:33.531 --> 00:03:36.201
in circles, lazily. They have no idea

00:03:36.201 --> 00:03:38.761
how to make their way around.

00:03:38.761 --> 00:03:41.421
Something interesting I saw a couple days ago,

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.011
the Nobel Prize in science just

00:03:43.011 --> 00:03:46.191
went to some researchers that identified

00:03:46.191 --> 00:03:48.590
something called the "internal GPS" within

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:52.221
cells. These cells are able to

00:03:52.221 --> 00:03:54.981
activate and stay activated only when an

00:03:54.981 --> 00:03:56.721
animal is facing in one particular

00:03:56.721 --> 00:03:58.551
direction. Which is how we're able to

00:03:58.551 --> 00:04:00.441
find our way around and remember where

00:04:00.441 --> 00:04:02.521
we've gone. We don't know if these cells

00:04:02.561 --> 00:04:04.841
are magneto receptive yet. But it

00:04:04.841 --> 00:04:07.241
makes sense that they would be.

00:04:07.241 --> 00:04:10.141
They're doing more research in that.

00:04:10.681 --> 00:04:13.081
I know what you're thinking is like,

00:04:13.181 --> 00:04:15.461
it seems impossible that we would have this sense

00:04:15.471 --> 00:04:16.911
when we can't find our way out of a

00:04:16.911 --> 00:04:18.621
shopping mall or parking lot.

00:04:18.621 --> 00:04:22.261
The fact is we just don't need it today

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:23.841
too much. But we did need it

00:04:23.841 --> 00:04:25.981
about 400 years ago, and before then.

00:04:26.161 --> 00:04:28.321
This is what Manhattan was supposed to

00:04:28.321 --> 00:04:31.241
look like about 400 years ago. You'd need

00:04:31.241 --> 00:04:32.861
a pretty good sense of direction to make

00:04:32.861 --> 00:04:34.931
it through here. And especially through

00:04:34.931 --> 00:04:37.801
the heavily forested areas. This is what

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:40.741
Manhattan looks like now. You need zero

00:04:40.821 --> 00:04:42.541
sense of direction to make it around

00:04:42.541 --> 00:04:45.641
here. The pattern of settlements, roads and

00:04:45.641 --> 00:04:47.681
other landmarks that undergrid

00:04:47.681 --> 00:04:50.141
our modern society make it easy to

00:04:50.141 --> 00:04:51.921
know exactly where we are.

00:04:51.921 --> 00:04:54.201
And of course if ever we're in doubt

00:04:54.201 --> 00:04:56.441
you pull out your phone. From practically

00:04:56.441 --> 00:04:58.601
anywhere on the planet you can see

00:04:58.601 --> 00:05:02.221
exactly where you are through GPS.

